    dcterms:created                                         "2019-03-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:issued                                          "2019-03-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified                                        "2026-11-16"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:publisher                                            "Linked.Archi"@en, <https://linked.archi> ;
    bibo:status                                             "draft" ;
    owl:versionIRI                                          <https://meta.linked.archi/core#> ;
    owl:versionInfo                                         "0.6.0"@en ;
    owl:priorVersion                                        <https://meta.linked.archi/core/0.5.0#> ;
    skos:historyNote                                        '''0.5.0 — names, labels and pictures per presentation context.
arch:inPresentationContext says which presentation context — which audience — something is for: a
name an element is given for that audience (a SKOS-XL label, skosxl:altLabel, whose plain form is
also the element's skos:altLabel), a picture of it for that audience (a schema:ImageObject given as
arch:altVisNotation), or, on a diagram, what its label says there (core-vis 0.7's
arch-vis:LabelExpression) and how it looks there (an arch-vis:Style). skos:prefLabel stays the one
canonical name and arch:prefVisNotation the one canonical picture. arch:prefVisNotation and
arch:altVisNotation say where they apply with :domainIncludes, where an rdfs:domain of skos:Concept
made every element given a picture a SKOS concept. See DD-34 and DD-35.

0.4.0 — membership properties reworked.
arch:inView and arch:inModel replace arch:exposedInView and arch:partOfModel, and arch:contains is
deprecated as an undeclared inverse of what was then partOfModel. All three old properties are
retained and owl:deprecated; the two renamed ones are rdfs:subPropertyOf their replacements so
existing data still entails the current vocabulary under RDFS, while arch:contains is not, because
no sound generalisation exists for it. See DD-30.'''@en ;
#        Vowl
